第二步：非谓语动词词组=起点+终点（前）
起点：to do；doing；done
终点=下一个标点符号前；下一个连接词前；
下一个动词前
无
第三步：一个连词+搭配一个谓语动词+终
点（下一个标点符号；下一个连接词；下
一个动词）', '英语2/语法基础第十节-定从1.pdf', 14, true, 7, null),
  ('3970a849-d40f-5c6b-a1e8-1b22c9ece7a3', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'Vaish holds that the rethinking about guilt comes from an awareness that ______. [A] emotions are context-independent 情绪与场景无关 [B] emotions are socially constructive情绪具有社会建设性 [C] emotional stability can benefit health情绪稳定有益于身体健康 [D] an emotion can play opposing roles 同一种情绪能够起到截然相反的作用 18 [D] an emotion can play opposing roles 分析选项：[A] emotions are context-independent（情感与情境无关）：与原文矛盾，原文强调情感的作用 取决于情境。[B] emotions are socially constructive（情感具有社会建设性）：原文未提到“社会建设性”， 属于无关信息。[C] emotional stability can benefit health（情绪稳定有益健康）：原文未提及“情绪稳定”或 “健康”，属于无关信息。[D] an emotion can play opposing roles（一种情感不同情况下可以扮演对立的角 色）：与原文完全一致，对应“may be advantageous in one context may be harmful in another”。排除法： [A]、[B]、[C]均与原文无关或矛盾，只有[D]直接对应原文。 opponent n.对手，竞争者；反对者，阻止者；adj.对立的，敌对的 opposite prep.在……对面，与……相对 阅读过程中碰到不认识的单词怎么办？？ 19 情况一：不懂的单词在核心观点句，利用后边句子帮助理解一下观点即可，不要陷入细节 In the popular imagination, of course, guilt still gets a bad rap. It is deeply uncomfortable—it’s the emotional equivalent of wearing a jacket weighted with stones. 情况二：通过连接词的关系，绕开它 There has been a kind of revival or a rethinking about what guilt is and what role guilt can serve 真题演练三 20 In the popular imagination, of course, guilt still gets a bad rap. It is deeply uncomfortable—it’s the emotional equivalent of wearing a jacket weighted with stones. Yet this understanding is outdated. “There has been a kind of revival or a rethinking about what guilt is and what role guilt can serve,” says Amrisha Vaish, a psychology researcher at the University of Virginia, adding that this revival is part of a larger recognition that emotions aren’t binary—feelings that may be advantageous in one context may be harmful in another. Jealousy and anger, for example, may have evolved to alert us to important inequalities. Too much happiness can be destructive. According to Paragraph 2, many people still consider guilt to be ______. [A] deceptive欺骗性的；误导的；虚伪的 [B] burdensome繁重的；令人不堪重负的；累赘的 [C] addictive使人上瘾的；易沉迷的 [D] inexcusable不可原谅的；无法辩解的 21 [B] burdensome 解题步骤：定位关键信息：第二段开头提到： In the popular imagination, of course, guilt still gets a bad rap. It is deeply uncomfortable—it’s the emotional equivalent of wearing a jacket weighted with stones. "gets a bad rap"：意思是内疚通常被负面看待。"deeply uncomfortable"和"wearing a jacket weighted with stones"：用“背着装满石头的夹克”比喻内疚的感受，强调其沉重、负担的特性。 分析选项：[A] deceptive（欺骗性的）：原文未提及内疚与欺骗相关。[B] burdensome（沉重的）：与 “wearing a jacket weighted with stones”（背着沉重的石头）直接对应，强调内疚是一种负担。[C] addictive（上瘾的）：原文未提及内疚会让人上瘾。[D] inexcusable（不可原谅的）：原文未提到内疚是 否可以被原谅。 定语从句阅读阅读方法：there指的是什么 22 "We are just in a situation where there are no good theories explaining what consciousness actually is and how you could ever build a machine to get there." 我们正处于这样一种困境：目前尚无完善的理论能解释意识的本质，也无法阐明如何打造 出（?)的机器。 第一步：找出所有动词 are， are，explaining，is，could build，to get 第二步：非谓语动词词组=起点+终点（前） 起点：to do；doing；done 终点=下一个标点符号前；下一个连接词前； 下一个动词前', null, '及解析', '', '英语2/语法基础第十节-定从1.pdf', 17, true, 8, null),
  ('8214ef2f-5734-540c-90b8-5e77d6dbf4cc', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', 'how you could ever build a machine 结论：唯一谓语动词are 主句：We are just in a situation 代词there指的是什么？ 23 ①Today the rapid growth of artificial intelligence (AI) raises fundamental questions: "What is intelligence, identity, or consciousness? What makes humans humans?" ②Just how people think is still far too complex to be understood, let alone reproduced, says David Eagleman, a Stanford University neuroscientist. "We are just in a situation where there are no good theories explaining what consciousness actually is and how you could ever build a machine to get there." there是地点隐喻，指代前文提出的目标状态 代词很大概率都是跟核心的复现词相关的，可从核心复现词入手 真题演练四，如果核心观点句里面有不认识得单词怎么办？ complex，reproduced—下文可能是上文观点的具象化解释 24 ①Today the rapid growth of artificial intelligence (AI) raises fundamental questions: "What is intelligence, identity, or consciousness? What makes humans humans?" ②Just how people think is still far too complex to be understood, let alone reproduced, says David Eagleman, a Stanford University neuroscientist. "We are just in a situation where there are no good theories explaining what consciousness actually is and how you could ever build a machine to get there." In David Eagleman''s opinion, our current knowledge of consciousness ______.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "helps explain artificial intelligence有助于解释人工智能"}, {"key": "B", "text": "can be misleading to robot making对机器人制造产生误导"}, {"key": "C", "text": "inspires popular sci-fi TV series给热门科幻电视剧带来创作灵感"}, {"key": "D", "text": "is too limited for us to reproduce it太过有限，我们无法复刻它（意识） 什么时候看上下文，用上下文解题？观点有不懂的单词或者观点难 以理解过于抽象"}]'::jsonb, '', '', '英语2/语法基础第十节-定从1.pdf', 22, true, 9, null),
  ('d71d6564-a342-548c-b9b2-c4cf8d68d6d8', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', '第二句：直接引语具象化解释（Explanation） 用专家的原话拆解为什么会有上面那个结论：现状 = 没有成熟理论定义意识本质，也不知道如何造出具备意识 的机器。 翻译：“我们当下的处境是，尚无完善理论能够阐释意识究竟是什么，更无从谈起如何制造一台拥有意识的机 器。” 解题：捉复现词+感情色彩no good 26 ①Today the rapid growth of artificial intelligence (AI) raises fundamental questions: "What is intelligence, identity, or consciousness? What makes humans humans?" ②Just how people think is still far too complex to be understood, let alone reproduced, says David Eagleman, a Stanford University neuroscientist. "We are just in a situation where there are no good theories explaining what consciousness actually is and how you could ever build a machine to get there." In David Eagleman''s opinion, our current knowledge of consciousness ______.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "helps explain artificial intelligence有助于解释人工智能"}, {"key": "B", "text": "can be misleading to robot making对机器人制造产生误导"}, {"key": "C", "text": "inspires popular sci-fi TV series给热门科幻电视剧带来创作灵感"}, {"key": "D", "text": "is too limited for us to reproduce it太过有限，我们无法复刻它（意识）"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '', '英语2/语法基础第十节-定从1.pdf', 25, false, 10, null),
  ('f42f2f95-035f-59d5-9ddf-446904880927', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', 'than they absorb 主干：The climate change could one day leave us with forests 真题演练五【Forests，we humans】 34 Forests give us shade, quiet and one of the harder challenges in the fight against climate change. Despite the fact that we humans count on forests to soak up a good share of the carbon dioxide we produce, we are threatening their ability to do so. The climate change we are hastening could one day leave us with forests that emit more carbon than they absorb. By saying "one of the harder challenges," the author implies that ______. [A] global climate change may get out of control全球气候变化可能会失控 [B] people may misunderstand global warming人们或许会误解全球变暖 [C] extreme weather conditions may arise极端天气状况可能出现 [D] forests may become a potential threat森林可能成为一种潜在威胁 35', '[{"key": "A", "text": "global climate change may get out of control（全球气候变化可能会失控） 原文只说：森林固碳能力受损，未来森林会碳释放＞碳吸收，加剧气候问题。 文中完全没有 “失控（out of control）” 这个程度的表述，属于过度夸大、无中生有。 题干提问对象是 “森林是难题”，A 的主语是气候变化，偏离核心讨论对象。"}, {"key": "B", "text": "people may misunderstand global warming（人们可能误解全球变暖） 全文没有任何句子提到 “人们误解、认知错误” 相关内容，整篇只讲人类破坏森林、森林固碳失效，完 全无对应信息，无中生有。"}, {"key": "C", "text": "extreme weather conditions may arise（极端天气可能会出现） 文章全程只围绕「森林、二氧化碳、碳吸收 / 排放」展开； 从头到尾没有出现高温、暴雨、台风、干旱等极端天气相关字眼，属于凭空捏造的信息，无中生有。 D 为什么正确原文关键句：forests that emit more carbon than they absorb 森林本是对抗气候变化的帮手，如今会反向释放碳，加重气候危机，等同于森林会变成潜在威胁，完全匹 配文意。 定语从句翻译 定语从句翻译:8大8小原则"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '', '英语2/语法基础第十节-定从1.pdf', 33, true, 11, null),
  ('772ba07e-70a0-548c-a5b4-5d41db48d00e', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'It can be learned that in Iowa，_____. [A] wind is a widely used energy source风能是一种被广泛使用的能源 [B] wind energy has replaced fossil fuels风能已经取代了化石燃料 [C] tech giants are investing in clean energy科技巨头正在投资清洁能源 [D] there is a shortage of clean energy supply清洁能源供应存在短缺 48', null, 'A', '选项A正确。原文明确提到爱荷华州“风力发电机星罗棋布”（wind turbines dot the fields），且风
电占全州发电量的36%（provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation），说明风能已被广泛利
用。
选项B错误。文中未提及风能“完全取代”化石燃料（replaced fossil fuels），仅强调其占比高，且特朗普
仍主张发展化石燃料。
