cent of positions on European corporate boards.', '英语2/长难句6-状语从句【预习版】.pdf', 35, false, 60, null),
  ('4e0d9358-1534-5ea8-ad4d-4d73550250c4', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'In the European corporate workplace, generally______. [A] women take the lead [B] men have the final say [C] corporate governance is overwhelmed [D] senior management is family-friendly overwhelm这个词重点掌握，真题高频词 41 Overwhelming majorities of both groups said（that） they believe（that） it is harder for young people today to get started in life than it was for earlier generations. 绝大多数两组人都认为，如今年轻人开始独立生活比前几代人更难 42', null, '[B] men have the final say', '原文核心信息：欧洲企业高层性别不平等（"not a gender-equality heaven"）。
关键数据：女性仅占董事会席位的 14%，高层职位 "overwhelmingly male"（绝大多数为男性）。
职场环境 "never be completely family-friendly"（对家庭不友好）除非女性参与高层决策。
选项分析：[A] women take the lead（女性主导）→ 与原文矛盾，原文强调男性占主导地位。
[B] men have the final say（男性掌握最终决定权）→ 符合原文“高层绝大多数为男性”的描述，且女性
参与决策不足。
[C] corporate governance is overwhelmed（公司治理不堪重负）→ 原文未提及“不堪重负”，属于无关
选项。
[D] senior management is family-friendly（高层管理对家庭友好）→ 原文明确说职场 "never
completely family-friendly"，直接排除。排除法：[A]、[C]、[D] 均与原文冲突或无支持，仅 [B] 与数据
和高层性别比例一致。
